 "indicator": {
  "definition": {
   "definition": "Food credit is a category of bank credit comprising advances by scheduled commercial banks to the Food Corporation of India, State Governments and State Co-operative agencies for food procurement operations; together with non-food credit it adds up to total bank credit. RBI compiles it from the fortnightly Form A return of all SCBs under Section 42(2) of the RBI Act, 1934, and publishes it as item 7a.1 'Food Credit' of the 'Scheduled Commercial Banks — Business in India' statement in the WSS/RBI Bulletin, in rupees crore. It is seasonal, moving with the procurement calendar, so its y-o-y growth swings widely.",
   "source_name": "RBI — A Handbook on RBI's Weekly Statistical Supplement, Section 4: SCB – Business in India (item 7a.1 Food Credit)",
   "source_url": "https://rbidocs.rbi.org.in/rdocs/Publications/PDFs/HWSSF170614.pdf",
